我们在那里呆了一个赛季。

00:36:20.630 --> 00:36:32.505
But basically, everything we needed to learn to be a showrunner, we learned at Letterman, and then when you go on to a sitcom staff, a lot of the ethos, at least back in the day when we were getting into it, was like, the writers weren't in the edit room.
但基本上，我们在莱特曼学到了成为一名剧集主管所需的一切，然后当你进入情景喜剧工作人员时，很多精神，至少在我们进入它的那天，就像，编剧不在编辑室里。

00:36:32.505 --> 00:36:34.647
The writers weren't necessarily always on set.
编剧不一定总是在片场。

00:36:34.647 --> 00:36:38.047
The writers sort of wrote things and were that part of the assembly line.
作家们写了一些东西，并且是流水线的一部分。

00:36:38.047 --> 00:36:48.153
On Letterman, you had, if you had an idea in the morning, you had to produce it by the showtime, you had to get your music, you had to order up your graphics, you had to, if there was, like, Kyron and titles involved.
在莱特曼，你必须，如果你早上有一个想法，你必须在放映时间之前制作它，你必须获得你的音乐，你必须订购你的图形，你必须，如果涉及到凯伦和标题。

00:36:48.153 --> 00:36:52.670
Every piece of it, you went on the shoot, you basically kind of directed or co-directed your bit.
每一个片段，你都参与拍摄，基本上都是你自己导演或共同导演的。

00:36:52.670 --> 00:36:56.070
You had it with the director and make sure you got everything you needed.
你和导演商定了，并确保你得到了你需要的一切。

00:36:56.070 --> 00:36:59.263
Get into an edit room, book your time there, get with the editor.
进入编辑室，预订时间，与编辑会面。

00:36:59.263 --> 00:37:00.737
Like every part of it was you.
就像它的每一部分都是你一样。

00:37:00.737 --> 00:37:03.292
Every part of it you were responsible for producing.
它的每个部分都是你负责制作的。

00:37:03.292 --> 00:37:05.995
And that was such good training for being a showrunner.
对于成为一名节目主持人来说，这真是一次很好的训练。

00:37:05.995 --> 00:37:11.842
Because by the time, I think by the time some writers who've only ever been on sitcom staffs, they become a showrunner.
因为到了那个时候，我认为到了一些只在情景喜剧工作人员中工作过的作家，他们就成为了剧集主管。

00:37:11.842 --> 00:37:15.969
They've never really spent a lot of of time in edit, they've never done a sound mix.
他们从未真正花费大量时间进行编辑，也从未进行过混音。

00:37:15.969 --> 00:37:18.710
I remember we had done all that stuff.
我记得我们已经做了所有这些事情。

00:37:18.710 --> 00:37:26.469
It can't be overstated how much like technology and like the editing software that exists now like I movie coming built into your laptop.
无论如何强调，它与现在存在的技术和编辑软件有多么相似，就像我的电影内置在你的笔记本电脑中一样。

00:37:26.469 --> 00:37:27.909
How much that has changed the world?
这给世界带来了多大改变？

00:37:27.909 --> 00:37:34.949
Because at the time it really was like us knowing how to go into an edit room was like we'd gone to Hogwarts.
因为当时我们知道如何进入编辑室就像我们去了霍格沃茨一样。

00:37:34.949 --> 00:37:43.469
Like we like had this like mystical power that like like really like no one understood how to like, you know trim 15 frames off of something.
就像我们喜欢拥有这种神秘的力量一样，就像没有人知道如何喜欢一样，你知道将某些东西剪掉 15 帧。

00:37:43.469 --> 00:37:57.880
Like dumb simple stuff that anyone in the world now knows, it was really like that letterman definitely gave us a chance to like basically go to film school for four years, go to film school and comedy school in a big way.
就像现在世界上任何人都知道的愚蠢简单的事情一样，这真的就像莱特曼确实给了我们一个机会，基本上可以去电影学校四年，在很大程度上去电影学校和喜剧学校。

00:37:57.880 --> 00:38:12.019
I also feel like the whole like 10,000 hours thing of like learning how to like I definitely feel like I learned how to how to write a joke and how to write something that gets a laugh.
我也觉得整个一万个小时的事情就像学习如何喜欢我绝对觉得我学会了如何写一个笑话以及如何写一些让人发笑的东西。

00:38:12.019 --> 00:38:21.739
I don't even think that myself isn't necessarily a funny person, but I knew what the mechanics were of, and the only way to learn that is doing it over and over and failing a lot.
我什至不认为自己不一定是一个有趣的人，但我知道其中的机制是什么，而学习这一点的唯一方法就是一遍又一遍地做，并多次失败。

00:38:21.739 --> 00:38:24.300
Yeah, I wanted to ask you about that.
是的，我想问你这个问题。

00:38:24.300 --> 00:38:40.632
The failure did it, it did it, thicken your skin considerably, so you pitch jokes, obviously, to these older, more veteran writers, and they're swatting them down, or ideas are getting bad a down or something doesn't get a laugh like did you feel like that which didn't kill you made you stronger kind of by the end of that.
失败做到了，它做到了，让你的脸皮变得厚厚的，所以你显然向这些年长、更有经验的作家开玩笑，他们正在猛烈地打压他们，或者想法变得很糟糕，或者有些事情不会让人笑，就像你觉得那些没有杀死你的东西到最后会让你变得更坚强。

00:38:40.632 --> 00:39:29.830
Yeah definitely and it was very humbling and it told you it was a volume business you needed to have an extra you needed to have an next idea there was no there's no writers block when you're doing five shows a week and you're getting paid decent money to do it there's no writer you have to have an idea you have to have an idea and even if it's not great you have to do you have to produce it and make it and hope that it gets on and does okay Carter and I did the viewer male segment for four years of our four and a half years there, and we would go down for the taping of that segment and be in the audience, and you had to sit in that, and we stood up to the side, and we would sit there and listen to those play and either get a laugh from the audience or not get a laugh from the audience, and what didn't get a laugh, and it was dead silent, and Dave's up there, this iconic, wonderful, I mean, I idolized Dave, I loved him, I made that joke before, but I loved Dave.
是的，这确实是非常令人谦卑的，它告诉你，这是一个批量业务，你需要额外的东西，你需要有下一个想法，没有作家的障碍，当你每周做五场演出，而且你得到了可观的钱来做这件事，没有作家，你必须有一个想法，你必须有一个想法，即使它不是很好，你也必须做，你必须制作它并制作它，并希望它能继续下去，做得很好卡特和我做了四个观众的男性部分我们在那四年半的时间里，我们会去录制那个片段，坐在观众席上，你必须坐在那儿，我们站到一边，我们会坐在那里听那些戏剧，要么让观众笑，要么不让观众笑，没有笑的，就一片寂静，戴夫就在那里，这个标志性的，美妙的，我的意思是，我崇拜戴夫，我爱他，我以前开过那个玩笑，但我爱戴夫。

00:39:29.830 --> 00:39:33.460
When he would turn on it, he'd go like, Ooh, that was a tough one, Paul.
当他打开它时，他会说，哦，这很难，保罗。

00:39:33.460 --> 00:39:39.860
I feel like we were getting torn a new one on national television by our hero, or at least my hero.
我觉得我们的英雄，或者至少是我的英雄，在国家电视台上撕扯了一场新的戏。

00:39:39.860 --> 00:39:41.593
And there's nothing more humbling.
没有什么比这更令人谦卑的了。

00:39:41.593 --> 00:39:44.500
There's no thicker skin to be developed than that moment.
没有比那一刻更厚的脸皮了。

00:39:44.500 --> 00:39:50.543
And you got to scrape yourself off the floor and say, I got at least one more shot at this next week if we don't get fired.
你必须把自己从地板上爬起来，说，如果我们不被解雇的话，下周我至少还有一次机会。

00:39:50.543 --> 00:39:52.017
And you just work even harder.
而你只是更加努力地工作。

00:39:52.017 --> 00:39:54.179
And you develop that ability to bounce back.
你就会培养出反弹的能力。

